* sg13g2-bandgap -- sg13cmos5l-closed-loop-startup bench body for the `klt sim`
* harness (issue #337, Part of #322). Instantiated by
* sim/sg13cmos5l-closed-loop-startup/run_klt_sim.sh, which substitutes @@OSDI_DIR@@, @@VDD@@
* (the ramp target) and @@MSENSE_W@@ (XMSENSE's width, read from the live
* design/sg13cmos5l/netlist/bandgap_startup.spice at run time, as the legacy
* run_pvt_sweep.sh does). Every device line is copied from the legacy
* tb_sg13cmos5l_closed_loop_startup.spice.tmpl, which is itself verbatim
* from design/sg13cmos5l/netlist/{bandgap_core,bandgap_amp,bandgap_startup}.spice,
* wired as design/sg13cmos5l/bandgap_top.sch specifies.
*
* `klt sim` netlist-body convention: this file is a circuit BODY. Moved out
* of the legacy template: the three `.lib` corner cards (selected per
* process corner by the request), `.options temp=T tnom=27` (`klt sim`
* emits the corner's `.temp`), and the `tran` / `meas` control commands
* (now the request's `analysis` and `measurements`).
*
* Same one deliberate deviation as every `klt sim` body in this repo: the
* `.control` preload block below (klayout-tools#2666).
.control
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/r3_cmc.osdi
.endc

* rshunt=1e9 / gmin=1e-9: convergence aids only, both far below any current
* measured here -- carried over unchanged from the legacy template (the
* real, not-yet-loop-gain-tuned amplifier can fail to converge at an early,
* near-singular instant on the vdd ramp at a marginal corner). The request
* `options` object has no engine-option passthrough, so the setting lives
* in the body.
.options rshunt=1e9 gmin=1e-9

* FIXTURE -- transient supply ramp: vdd itself ramps 0 -> VDD over 200 us
* and holds to 2 ms, so the assembled block's own cold-start ->
* closed-loop-settled transition is what the simulator solves for. The ramp
* target is baked into this body (@@VDD@@), because a PWL source cannot be
* swept with `alter`: run_klt_sim.sh therefore dispatches one request per
* supply (the request carries no supply axis).
Vvdd vdd 0 PWL(0 0 200u @@VDD@@ 2m @@VDD@@)
Vvss vss 0 dc 0
* The core's rppd bulk terminals reach the global substrate net `sub!`;
* tied to vss through a 0 V source, as in the legacy template.
Vsub sub! vss dc 0

* DUT -- design/sg13cmos5l/netlist/bandgap_core.spice, verbatim.
* Grounded-collector pnpMPA legs (base+collector at vss, emitter at the
* sense node).
XM1 sns1 fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XQ1 vss vss sns1 pnpMPA a={ 1u * 2u } p={ ( 1u + 2u ) * 2 } m=1
XM2 sns2 fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XR2 sns2 e2 sub! rppd w=2u l=85.1u m=1 b=0
XQ2 vss vss e2 pnpMPA a={ 1u * 2u } p={ ( 1u + 2u ) * 2 } m=8
XM3 vref fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XR1 vref e3 sub! rppd w=2u l=647.0u m=1 b=0
XQ3 vss vss e3 pnpMPA a={ 1u * 2u } p={ ( 1u + 2u ) * 2 } m=1

* DUT -- design/sg13cmos5l/netlist/bandgap_amp.spice, verbatim. in_p <-
* sns2 (non-inverting), in_n <- sns1 (inverting), out -> fb.
XMTAIL tail fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMP1 d1 sns2 tail vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=20u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMP2 d2 sns1 tail vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=20u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMP3 pn pn vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMP4 fb pn vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMN1 d1 d1 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMN2 d2 d2 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMN3 fb d1 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMN4 pn d2 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1

* DUT -- design/sg13cmos5l/netlist/bandgap_startup.spice, verbatim. `sns1`
* and `fb` are shared with the core and amp DUTs above; no separate stimulus
* source drives either.
*
* FIXTURE -- Vmkfb is a 0 V ammeter in series with XMKFB's drain, so the
* startup circuit's own contribution to the shared fb node is measured
* directly (i_mkfb_final_a). A 0 V source is a DC/transient short.
XRPU vdd det sub! rhigh w=1u l=1411.3u m=1 b=0
XMSENSE det sns1 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=@@MSENSE_W@@ l=0.5u ng=1 m=1
Vmkfb fb fbx dc 0
XMKFB fbx det vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=2u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1
